& [Observed]
  + the first PowerShell7 live-evidence fixture rejected a valid UTC provider creation instant and later changed receipt bytes while recomputing its self digest

& [Cause]
  + PowerShell7 ConvertFrom-Json materializes ISO date strings as DateTime while WindowsPowerShell5.1 retains strings; object reserialization is therefore not a stable cross-host byte-custody operation

& [Correction]
  + normalize DateTime only for semantic UTC validation and recompute the receipt digest by replacing the exact terminal digest value in the retained raw UTF-8 record
  + retain native raw plan and verification byte comparisons instead of round-tripping those artifacts through host JSON objects

& [Verification]
  + PowerShell7 and WindowsPowerShell5.1 each pass the complete fixture and four isolated refusals with remote_calls0 effects0

& [Effect]
  + only generated provider-free fixture roots were involved and safely removed; no package byte remote state or authority boundary changed
